WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:06.190
Ask Ken to TLC. Nippongo is hard, tenses are hard sometimes, and I might fuck up.

00:11.590 --> 00:13.970
The entire south building is our playground.

00:13.970 --> 00:15.230
Four people will defend.

00:15.230 --> 00:19.970
If the other six manage to kick the can, or remain uncaught until time runs out, they win.

00:25.060 --> 00:25.640
Let's go!

00:25.640 --> 00:27.350
Let the Kick-The-Can Competition commence!

00:33.830 --> 00:35.610
Haru-chin feels refreshed!

00:37.680 --> 00:40.080
Wh-what the hell do you think you’re doing?!

00:41.580 --> 00:42.900
Um...

00:42.900 --> 00:45.420
Weren't you supposed to be a defender, Saigusa-san?

00:45.420 --> 00:46.790
I am.

00:47.500 --> 00:50.170
So what happens if the defender kicks the can?

00:50.290 --> 00:52.300
Well...

00:52.420 --> 00:54.340
I think it's called "self-destruction."

00:55.240 --> 00:56.670
And thus the winners are...

00:57.540 --> 00:58.470
Riki's team!

00:58.470 --> 01:00.050
Yay!

01:00.050 --> 01:02.110
I can't accept this!

01:02.110 --> 01:05.330
Well, you know when you see someone eating something that looks really good,

01:05.330 --> 01:08.980
don't you just get that urge to zoom up from the side to snatch it away and eat it?

01:08.980 --> 01:11.320
It's the same as that!

01:11.320 --> 01:12.360
Capital punishment.

01:13.480 --> 01:15.280
Please wait, Anego...

01:15.280 --> 01:18.680
I won't do it again!

01:20.490 --> 01:21.290
There she is!

01:21.290 --> 01:22.780
Saigusa Haruka!

01:22.780 --> 01:23.740
Yikes!

01:28.120 --> 01:31.860
You were supposed to be picking up empty cans during lunch break as punishment.

01:33.210 --> 01:34.920
Well...

01:35.510 --> 01:37.620
I was actually doing just that!

01:37.620 --> 01:38.550
See?

01:38.970 --> 01:40.600
It really does appear that way.

01:40.600 --> 01:41.880
Escape!

01:41.880 --> 01:43.720
Stop right there!

01:43.720 --> 01:45.680
You're the ones who should stop.

01:46.760 --> 01:51.010
What good is it to violate the very rules that you're trying to protect?

01:51.010 --> 01:53.570
Please be quiet within school grounds, especially in the hallways.

01:54.020 --> 01:55.550
Chairman...

01:55.550 --> 01:57.830
We're really sorry.

02:00.970 --> 02:03.950
Haruka, make sure to collect the empty cans after school today.

02:04.960 --> 02:06.080
Yes, ma'am.

02:08.490 --> 02:11.580
The rest of you too, make sure you don't cause too much of a ruckus.

02:12.340 --> 02:13.840
Let's go.

02:19.030 --> 02:20.420
Scary.

02:20.420 --> 02:22.220
Even though they've settled the issues between them as siblings,

02:22.220 --> 02:24.760
it's not like everything's all well and dandy.

02:27.390 --> 02:29.520
As the Public Morals Chairman,

02:29.880 --> 02:32.800
Futaki-san was always someone to be feared.

02:52.300 --> 02:59.140
Presented By Refrain Subs!

03:02.810 --> 03:08.690
Since being alone was tough, the two of us held hands.

03:09.190 --> 03:15.200
The two of us were lonely, so we all stood in a circle and joined hands.

03:15.160 --> 03:23.410
I'm sure that's where we will gather our strength.

03:23.330 --> 03:28.380
Enough to stand up to any dream.

03:28.250 --> 03:31.010
Fly high towards the sky,

03:30.670 --> 03:35.180
Kick off the ground and send your voice to the heavens,

03:34.880 --> 03:40.220
Until you overcome those painful days.

03:40.010 --> 03:45.350
I'll never forget your voice, and I'll never forget your tears.

03:44.980 --> 03:52.320
The future that we call "hope" begins now.

03:52.070 --> 04:03.120
Your feet will continue to step onward, even when the time of grief comes.

04:08.400 --> 04:09.810
We'll lose our club room?

04:09.810 --> 04:10.620
Why?

04:10.640 --> 04:15.320
Victory

04:10.640 --> 04:15.320
Aim for Koshien

04:11.740 --> 04:15.330
During the sports meeting, the topic of redistribution of the club rooms was brought up.

04:15.330 --> 04:17.930
Our club room might be one of those.

04:17.930 --> 04:18.790
That's how it is.

04:19.440 --> 04:20.710
Is that so?

04:20.710 --> 04:22.320
Don't be so down about it.

04:20.730 --> 04:28.740
Aim for Koshien

04:22.320 --> 04:27.010
Although we're just borrowing this room, it's still an important place for the Little Busters.

04:27.010 --> 04:28.980
We can't lose it.

04:28.740 --> 04:28.870
Aim for Koshien

04:28.980 --> 04:30.060
What are you going to do?

04:32.160 --> 04:34.520
I'm planning to settle this politically.

04:34.520 --> 04:35.770
Which means?

04:35.770 --> 04:37.320
You'll help out the Dormitory Council.

04:37.320 --> 04:40.900
It seems they’re lacking the manpower right now and need assistance.

04:40.900 --> 04:43.680
Helping them out will earn us some good points.

04:43.680 --> 04:45.450
The Student Council won't be able to ignore our request.

04:45.470 --> 04:53.480
Victory

04:45.470 --> 04:45.550
Aim for Koshien

04:45.720 --> 04:48.920
So we're basically using that as our point of negotiations for our club room.

04:45.800 --> 04:45.930
Aim for Koshien

04:48.920 --> 04:51.900
I've already asked everyone else to do other jobs.

04:50.180 --> 04:50.300
Aim for Koshien

04:51.900 --> 04:53.500
So Riki, can I leave it to you?

04:53.500 --> 04:54.580
Yeah.

04:54.580 --> 04:57.330
This is a mission too, right?

04:57.870 --> 04:59.060
That's right!

04:59.060 --> 04:59.960
Then let's begin.

05:00.330 --> 05:01.880
Mission Start!

05:02.610 --> 05:04.240
Dorm Head's Room

05:04.280 --> 05:06.460
Monthly                                    Calendar

05:05.190 --> 05:06.470
Sorry for intruding.

05:06.800 --> 05:07.420
There you are.

05:07.420 --> 05:08.300
We've been waiting.

05:10.050 --> 05:11.320
Naoe Riki?

05:11.320 --> 05:12.810
Futaki-san.

05:13.190 --> 05:16.940
I'm guessing you're worried that having just me here isn't enough.

05:16.940 --> 05:18.190
That's not true.

05:18.190 --> 05:20.320
I asked Natsume-kun for a favor.

05:20.320 --> 05:21.650
All right, just sit down over here.

05:22.000 --> 05:24.120
Take this seal and stamp it here like this.

05:35.580 --> 05:37.830
Well then, I'll be heading out for a bit.

05:38.710 --> 05:40.010
I'll patrol around the dorm.

05:40.010 --> 05:41.910
If anyone drops by, hear them out,

05:41.910 --> 05:45.010
and on the off chance nobody does, take it easy and drink some tea.

05:45.010 --> 05:46.840
Watch over the room for me, 'kay?

05:55.220 --> 05:57.430
Finally done!

06:02.380 --> 06:03.760
Need some help?

06:04.300 --> 06:05.980
It's fine. I'll do it myself.

06:16.860 --> 06:18.250
This is good.

06:21.980 --> 06:24.070
To Dorm Head:

06:21.980 --> 06:24.070
Thanks for all your kindnesso

06:21.980 --> 06:24.070
Noumi

06:22.700 --> 06:24.090
Oh, It's Kud's tea.

06:29.590 --> 06:30.840
What's wrong?

06:32.200 --> 06:33.720
Nothing.

06:38.060 --> 06:39.020
Do you have nothing else to do?

06:39.460 --> 06:42.190
If you put it that way, no I don't.

06:42.190 --> 06:44.230
If you're free, then why don't you go somewhere else?

06:44.230 --> 06:45.730
"Time is money."

06:45.730 --> 06:49.530
You can never take back even an instant of wasted time.

06:49.880 --> 06:53.160
You should have other things you need to do, right?

06:53.600 --> 06:57.830
I was asked to help out, so it's not like I can just leave like that.

06:57.830 --> 06:59.820
I'm here, aren't I? It's fine.

06:59.820 --> 07:02.830
And keeping watch over the room isn't really a job.

07:02.830 --> 07:04.710
That's irresponsible of you to say.

07:06.060 --> 07:09.090
I'll stay until the dorm leader gets back.

07:10.140 --> 07:11.670
Do whatever you want.

07:27.680 --> 07:28.650
What?

07:29.500 --> 07:30.860
Do you need anything?

07:30.860 --> 07:32.960
It's rude to just stare at me like that.

07:33.500 --> 07:35.300
S-Sorry.

07:37.380 --> 07:39.280
Are you almost done with that?

07:41.040 --> 07:43.880
Please don't make such an annoyed face.

07:43.880 --> 07:46.000
But I really <i>am</i> annoyed.

07:47.990 --> 07:50.050
Since I'm free, I'll help you out.

07:50.050 --> 07:51.740
Naoe Riki...

07:51.740 --> 07:53.460
You really are a man of leisure.

07:53.460 --> 07:55.470
Or are you trying to gain a favor?

07:55.470 --> 07:57.660
Do you have some other motive?

07:57.660 --> 08:00.360
No, I really just want to help you out.

08:00.360 --> 08:04.270
And instead of doing it alone, I'm sure we'll finish faster if we do it together.

08:08.770 --> 08:11.460
Look for the files listed here and pull them out.

08:11.460 --> 08:12.220
All right.

08:15.080 --> 08:16.100
What's this?

08:16.100 --> 08:18.030
It's a list of students who are dropping out.

08:18.030 --> 08:19.510
Dropping out?

08:19.510 --> 08:21.430
There's quite a few here.

08:21.430 --> 08:23.620
Somewhat of a lonely task, isn't it?

08:24.150 --> 08:26.670
Lonely?

08:26.670 --> 08:27.660
Yeah.

08:27.660 --> 08:30.640
I mean, they all went to the same school.

08:32.480 --> 08:33.940
Those are just empty sentiments.

08:34.590 --> 08:40.430
You should only be able to count on one hand how many people you would truly miss.

08:42.090 --> 08:43.900
That's not...

08:43.900 --> 08:45.900
Are you saying everyone is important to you?

08:46.650 --> 08:48.760
Can you remember every last one of them?

08:50.660 --> 08:54.340
Of course not. There's no way I can remember every one of them.

08:58.640 --> 09:00.920
But even so, when someone disappears,

09:00.920 --> 09:04.880
there's no way you won't feel a bit lonely.

09:04.880 --> 09:06.660
Don't you think so too, Futaki-san?

09:06.940 --> 09:08.170
I don't.

09:11.880 --> 09:13.960
Other people are of no concern to me.

09:14.550 --> 09:17.320
As long as I can protect what's important to me,

09:17.810 --> 09:19.270
then nothing else matters.

09:22.040 --> 09:23.840
Even if someone disappears,

09:23.840 --> 09:25.510
no one will notice—

09:25.510 --> 09:27.560
just like a casted pebble.

09:30.480 --> 09:31.620
I'm back!

09:31.620 --> 09:33.230
Good work, both of you!

09:33.230 --> 09:36.070
Thanks for today, A-chan-senpai.

09:36.070 --> 09:37.280
Then, I'll be leaving.

09:37.280 --> 09:38.590
Ah, wait a bit.

09:38.590 --> 09:40.160
Wanna eat some muffins?

09:40.160 --> 09:42.840
The Cafeteria ladies gave me some.

09:42.840 --> 09:44.370
I'll pass.

09:44.370 --> 09:46.670
I don't like sweet things.

09:46.670 --> 09:48.790
Would you please remember that already?

09:52.900 --> 09:54.250
Oh, my.

09:54.530 --> 09:57.620
Futaki-san isn't very talkative, is she?

09:58.980 --> 10:01.470
I'll refrain from commenting on that.

10:05.850 --> 10:07.640
Good work today, Riki-kun.

10:08.240 --> 10:11.140
Saigusa-san, you're actually picking up those empty cans.

10:11.140 --> 10:11.890
I guess so.

10:11.890 --> 10:15.140
Every can picked up is a benefit for our club room.

10:15.140 --> 10:17.050
Is this even related to our club room?

10:17.050 --> 10:18.140
Of course!

10:18.140 --> 10:21.490
We have to fulfill our obligations before claiming our rights.

10:21.490 --> 10:23.240
It's not just punishment!

10:23.660 --> 10:24.950
I see.

10:26.450 --> 10:29.460
Though I'm only repeating
what my onee-chan told me.

10:30.880 --> 10:32.540
The other party has been decided.

10:33.230 --> 10:34.000
I see.

10:34.500 --> 10:36.700
You don't seem surprised.

10:36.700 --> 10:38.780
That was the initial agreement.

10:39.390 --> 10:41.300
Have you told Haruka-san about this?

10:42.520 --> 10:44.160
My sister doesn't know.

10:48.020 --> 10:49.740
There's no need for her to know.

11:00.680 --> 11:03.090
It’s already summer, huh?

11:03.090 --> 11:04.960
It sure is.

11:05.760 --> 11:10.290
Would you guys please stay off of the lawn past lunch hours?

11:10.290 --> 11:12.400
O-Oh, I'm sorry!

11:12.400 --> 11:14.770
I'm not telling you to leave immediately. In fact...

11:14.770 --> 11:17.470
It would really help if you could remove any pebbles you find on the lawn.

11:19.080 --> 11:20.730
What are you doing?

11:20.730 --> 11:22.570
Lawn maintenance.

11:22.570 --> 11:24.510
We've already replaced one portion of it, but...

11:24.510 --> 11:26.520
It's starting to grow uneven here.

11:26.520 --> 11:29.520
So the public morals committee maintains the lawn too...

11:29.520 --> 11:31.700
Yeah, together with the gardening club.

11:31.700 --> 11:34.550
Oh I see, I had no idea.

11:34.550 --> 11:37.480
We get here early every morning to water it.

11:37.480 --> 11:39.780
Well, it's just part of our job.

11:39.780 --> 11:41.530
It's fine if no one else notices.

11:41.530 --> 11:44.320
Kanata-kun, aren't you hot in that jacket?

11:46.170 --> 11:48.490
I'm not too bothered by the heat.

11:49.440 --> 11:50.700
Goodbye.

11:54.060 --> 11:57.170
So she really doesn't like being seen.

12:14.600 --> 12:15.140
What?

12:15.140 --> 12:16.930
Huh? What is it?

12:16.930 --> 12:18.490
Stop standing around.

12:18.490 --> 12:22.490
We still have to tidy up the desks, wipe the dorm windows,

12:22.490 --> 12:24.980
and clean out the laundry room after this.

12:24.980 --> 12:28.280
Don't you think that's a little too much for us?

12:28.280 --> 12:31.470
Didn't I already tell you it's fine if you bring someone else to help out?

12:31.470 --> 12:35.740
Plus, you're the one who said it would be easier with two people.

12:36.460 --> 12:40.960
I felt like it would be a bother to you if I brought someone.

12:42.510 --> 12:46.000
Am I really that uneasy around others?

12:46.000 --> 12:46.780
N-No way!

12:46.780 --> 12:49.460
That's not what I meant.

12:49.460 --> 12:51.970
But it's definitely not your forte.

12:54.630 --> 12:55.730
You're right.

12:55.830 --> 12:58.720
Saigusa

12:56.190 --> 13:00.750
I'm not really used to being lively around others...

13:07.950 --> 13:11.400
But I really do enjoy watching others cause a commotion.

13:11.400 --> 13:12.690
Is that true?

13:12.690 --> 13:15.330
Yeah, and you guys are the best example of that.

13:15.330 --> 13:18.310
Whether it's baseball, Kick-The-Can, or a test of courage...

13:18.310 --> 13:21.170
You all have fun like infantile idiots.

13:21.500 --> 13:24.430
I feel like we have a lot to apologize for.

13:24.430 --> 13:25.720
Isn't it fine?

13:25.720 --> 13:29.000
School isn't all about fun and games.

13:29.000 --> 13:32.010
There's pain and sadness as well.

13:32.300 --> 13:34.630
There are even times when you'll get hurt.

13:35.740 --> 13:36.980
But even then...

13:38.530 --> 13:43.650
Even then, it's reassuring to be able to find fun moments among that.

13:46.500 --> 13:48.640
It's fine to play around, isn't it?

13:48.640 --> 13:50.320
While we still have the time...

13:50.950 --> 13:52.980
Dorm Head's Room

13:53.390 --> 13:55.240
We finished repairing the bulletin board.

13:55.240 --> 13:56.150
Good work!

13:56.150 --> 13:57.120
I've been waiting for you two!

13:59.800 --> 14:02.280
Why is she asking you to help out, too?

14:02.280 --> 14:04.130
Am I that unreliable?

14:04.130 --> 14:06.850
It's probably because that makes carrying the bags easier.

14:06.850 --> 14:08.060
So that's it.

14:08.060 --> 14:10.720
In that case, I won't refuse your help.

14:19.750 --> 14:21.640
Specializing in Keys

